  "facts": [
    "The Tauern Road Tunnel, stretching 6,546 m, ranks among Austria's longest road tunnels and opened its first bore in 1975, before the second tube was completed in 2010.",
    "A 1999 fire, sparked by a truck collision with a traffic‑signal column, claimed twelve lives and forced a three‑month closure, prompting extensive safety upgrades.",
    "The tunnel links the northern municipality of Flachau in St. Johann im Pongau with southern Zederhaus in Tamsweg, traversing the Radstadt Tauern range."
